    {
      "id": "rtdb.operator.index",
      "kind": "operator",
      "engine": "rtdb",
      "reference": "https://firebase.google.com/docs/database/security/rules-conditions",
      "status": "unprobed",
      "note": "Production accepts `[]` ONLY on the auth token map (`auth.token['admin']`, dynamic keys included). It REJECTS an array literal in an expression outright (deploying `[10, 100, 1000][plan]` fails with `Unexpected array literal.`), so an array literal is legal only as a `hasChildren([...])` argument; and it rejects indexing a snapshot value (`data.val()['plan']` fails with `No such method/property 'plan'`), so `.child()` is the only way into a snapshot. The repo grammar (RtdbExpr.ohm CallExpr_indexAccess) is broader than production. Observed by deploy-acceptance probe against the live oracle database while capturing rules-rtdb-r9-quota-math / r12-claims-and-server-time."
    },
